  "notes": "FORMATION:\n{破|は} (break, destroy) + {局|きょく} (situation, state) → broken situation\n\nVERB FORM:\n{破局|はきょく}する (to break up - for relationships)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {別|わか}れる (to break up, to part - more casual)\n- {別離|べつり} (separation, parting)\n- {崩壊|ほうかい} (collapse)\n- {破綻|はたん} (failure, bankruptcy)\n\nMEDIA USAGE:\n{破局|はきょく} is commonly used in entertainment news and tabloids when reporting on celebrity breakups. It sounds more dramatic than simple {別|わか}れる.",
